mt-secsgem
==========

The SECS-II stream/function layouts, data item meanings and ack codes, the GEM state models, and
the HSMS header layout in this crate were derived by reading the source of

  secsgem - Python SECS/GEM implementation
  https://github.com/bparzella/secsgem
  Copyright (c) 2013-2024 Benjamin Parzella
  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version

and porting the relevant behaviour to Rust. secsgem's license permits use under later versions of
the LGPL and conversion to the GNU GPL; this crate is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. No SEMI standard
text is reproduced. secsgem (version 0.3.0) was also used, unmodified, as a cross-check peer
during development; none of it is included in this repository.

SECS/GEM, SECS-II and HSMS are SEMI standards (E5, E30, E37). This crate is an independent
implementation, not affiliated with or endorsed by SEMI.
